    "body": "## Summary\n\nReplace `fmaxf(x, 0)` with `x + fabsf(x)` in the SM90 FP8 MQA logits epilogue, recovering the 2\u00d7 throughput gap between FMNMX (half-rate) and FADD (full-rate) on Hopper. The factor-of-2 introduced by the identity is resolved by folding `0.5f` into the existing `scale_kv` multiply \u2014 zero extra instructions, bit-exact numerics.\n\n## Background\n\nOn SM90, `fmaxf(x, 0)` compiles to a single FMNMX, which issues at 64 ops/clk/SM \u2014 half the rate of FADD/FFMA (128 ops/clk/SM). Meanwhile `x + |x|` compiles to a single FADD with the absolute-value operand modifier, which is a free encoding bit in the instruction word:\n\n```\nFADD R3, R3, |R3|    ; one instruction, full rate (cuobjdump, sm_90a)\n```\n\nThe relu executes once per `(token, head, kv)` score element in the MQA logits epilogue, so at 64 vs 128 ops/clk/SM the FMNMX form doubles the FP32 pipe time spent on relu alone.\n\nSince `x + |x| = 2 \u00b7 relu(x)` holds exactly for all finite IEEE-754 floats (`+0` for x \u2264 0), the doubled sum is simply halved by folding `* 0.5f` into the already-existing `scale_kv` multiplication (an exponent decrement, also exact):\n\n```cpp\n// Before:\nreturn fmaxf(shifted_accum[j], 0) * weights[i][(j / 4) * 2 + (j & 1)];\n...\nfloat v_0 = (sum[0] + sum[1]) * scale_kv_0;\n\n// After:\nreturn (shifted_accum[j] + fabsf(shifted_accum[j])) * weights[i][(j / 4) * 2 + (j & 1)];\n...\nfloat v_0 = (sum[0] + sum[1]) * (scale_kv_0 * 0.5f);\n```\n\nThe same technique is already used by the SM100 kernel (`sm100_mqa_logits.cuh`, packed `FADD2` variant); this PR brings it to SM90. Verified via `cuobjdump -sass`: zero FMNMX across all JIT-instantiated `sm90_fp8_mqa_logits` cubins.\n\n## Performance (H200, 132 SMs, SM90A)\n\nProduction indexer shapes, best of 3 reps, before \u2192 after:\n\n| Shape | Before | After | Gain |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| H=32, D=128, SQ=512, SKV=140k, FP32 logits | 1018 TFLOPS | 1093 TFLOPS | +7.4% |\n| SQ=512, SKV=130560, H=64, BF16, CP=1 | 1042 TFLOPS | 1126 TFLOPS | +8.1% |\n| SQ=512, SKV=130560, H=32, BF16, CP=0 | 941 TFLOPS | 989 TFLOPS | +5.1% |\n| SQ=2048, SKV=8192, H=64, BF16, CP=1 | 980 TFLOPS | 1027 TFLOPS | +4.8% |\n\nFull `tests/test_attention.py` sweep (192 contiguous MQA cases on SM90): **avg +3.7%** (SK=65536 subset +4.4%, H=64 subset +5.5%, best case +11.3%). Gains scale with the relu's share of kernel time: larger SKV, more heads, smaller head dim \u2192 bigger win. Paged MQA logits (separate kernel, untouched) is unaffected.\n\n## Correctness\n\n- `x + |x| = 2 \u00b7 relu(x)` exactly for all finite IEEE-754 floats (x > 0: `x + x = 2x`; x \u2264 0: `x + (\u2212x) = +0`); the \u00f72 via `* 0.5f` is an exact exponent decrement.\n- All 192 SM90 cases in `tests/test_attention.py` pass (numeric diff vs simulated reference, 20\u00d7 bitwise self-consistency, mask equality) \u2014 verified on H200.\n- NaN semantics differ (`x + |x|` propagates NaN; `fmaxf(NaN, 0)` returns 0), but WGMMA accumulator outputs are finite in practice; this matches the SM100 kernel's existing behavior.\n\n## Changes\n\n`deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm90_fp8_mqa_logits.cuh` \u2014 3 lines modified (transform lambda + two `* 0.5f` folds).\n",
